ssword", "type_raw": "LPWSTRlpszPassword"}, {"declaration_match": false, "description": "Specifies the state of the password. The system password can be active for the logon process and the password can be active for a screen saver. The following table shows the possible values. Value Description PASSWORD_STATUS_ACTIVE Makes the system password active. If this bit is not set, the password is disabled. PASSWORD_STATUS_SCREENSAVERPROTECT Makes the password active for a screen saver. When this is set it causes the startup screen to be displayed when a screen saver is deactivated by the user. If this bit is not set, no startup screen is displayed when the screen saver is deactivated by a user. The PASSWORD_STATUS_ACTIVE flag must also be set to set this flag.", "direction": null, "documented_values": [{"description": "Makes the system password active. If this bit is not set, the password is disabled.", "token": "PASSWORD_STATUS_ACTIVE"}, {"description": "Makes the password active for a screen saver. When this is set it causes the startup screen to be displayed when a screen saver is deactivated by the user. If this bit is not set, no startup screen is displayed when the screen saver is deactivated by a user. The PASSWORD_STATUS_ACTIVE flag must also", "token": "PASSWORD_STATUS_SCREENSAVERPROTECT"}], "evidence_status": "documented", "name": "dwStatus", "position": null, "type": null, "type_raw": null}, {"declaration_match": false, "description": "Pointer to a null-terminated string containing the password.", "direction": null, "documented_values": [], "evidence_status": "documented", "name": "lpszPassword", "position": null, "type": null, "type_raw": null}], "parse": {"model": "c_declarator_v1", "notes": ["unnamed_parameter:1", "unnamed_parameter:2"], "status": "parsed"}, "return_type": "BOOL", "schema_version": 1, "scope": null, "source": {"document_last_updated": null, "page_id": "ms891976", "page_path": "docs/mslearn/windows-ce-5.0/ms891976.html", "source_id": "mslear